{"name":"factions_greyish_warship","seed":118,"config":{"rivalsByCount":true}}
# Phase E4: a landed grey warship at work. New Expedition seed 118 with
# Rival factions 3 (as factions_greyish, on another seed): the greyish scout
# fl1 lands first on its landfall (sys_80, on the rim, under the mothership
# fl2, so a jump there is an interception), lifts off and lands on day 20 on
# Murk Basin (sys_5, a desert planet). Murk Basin has a close neighbour,
# Quiet Canyon (sys_56, 37 fuel from the Wreck Site, 8 from Murk Basin):
# jump there (day 13) and park, no ship met (the scout was still landed when
# the jump began), then debug days 7 to day 20, the scout landed on Murk
# Basin. Now,
# before the short hop, debug ship makes it a warship (its hold
# emptied, so the trip's digging does not send it home) of eight that
# knows the armory module, field emitter, beam weapons, cloning and the
# research array; it is edited where it stands, since a warship made at its
# landfall picks another site. Hop to Murk Basin (3 days, day 23) and it is still
# landed, early in its stay, so it lands with its modules (vat, console, armory, two
# emitters), its array built on the ground, three workers, two technicians,
# two soldiers with beam rifles and a heavy. Beam one colonist down, set the
# greys neutral (the landing's contact turns them hostile; the emitters
# would shoot the colonist) and look: the camp, then a day of work (mining,
# digging, research). Then end its stay: it lifts off and leaves a landing
# scar (no hull, no modules) with its array as a wreck.
